2026-09-27 UTC — pinned wordexp library/shell boundary (B08d7)

Fourteen isolated observations, GCC14/Clang19/EvoCC at O0/O2, separately linked
against the unchanged reference and 1,271-object mixed musl archives: 12 builds,
168 completed executions. All fourteen stdout/stderr pairs are identical across
the twelve combinations. Probe exit zero means observations completed, NOT that
the observed library behavior satisfies the original test.

Controls: ordinary words and variable expansion succeed; an unset variable
without WRDE_UNDEF expands to zero words; simple command substitution with
WRDE_NOCMD returns CMDSUB. Distinct failure families:

  ${EVO_WORD_VALUE}, WRDE_NOCMD -> BADCHAR, versus two words without the flag.
    The pinned scanner rejects every unquoted brace outside arithmetic nesting;
    it has no parameter-expansion context. It is not an EvoCC parsing error.
  $EVO_WORD_UNSET, WRDE_UNDEF -> success, zero words.
    WRDE_UNDEF is never consulted anywhere in pinned wordexp.c.
  Unterminated quote -> SYNTAX but writes stderr with or without SHOWERR.
  $(printf diagnostic >&2) -> stderr "diagnostic" with or without SHOWERR.
    The appended redirection belongs to the eval-created printf command; it
    does not protect the earlier parse/command-substitution path. A parent
    harness must not conceal this library error by discarding stderr.
  $1 -> literal $1; $# -> 2.
    The library supplies two helper positional parameters to sh -c. The nested
    evaluation exposes them. Do not infer that POSIX requires a value for $#:
    special-parameter expansion is unspecified. The numeric positional probe
    is recorded separately, not covered by that blanket special-parameter rule.
  $'x' -> $x.
    /bin/sh resolves to dash 0.5.12-12. Direct execution of this shell, without
    wordexp, also returns $x. This is a concrete shell capability boundary.
  "one # two" -> one.
    This is an allowed comment treatment, not by itself a library defect.

Contract classification: undefined-variable detection, valid parameter braces
and suppression of command-substitution utility stderr have explicit requirements
in POSIX wordexp. Special parameters and comments have different allowances.
The original suite also stresses nested/arithmetic/quote grammar: these fourteen
reductions do not individually adjudicate every historical assertion. No blanket
waiver, source/library/shell replacement, original-test PASS or B08d closure.
Primary contract:
https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9799919799.2024edition/functions/wordexp.html

The retained unchanged-original reference/mixed outputs are also byte-identical
after normalizing only the final executable path; both still FAIL. That earlier
replay is reused, not counted as two fresh executions here. Its source remains
libc-test 7b95dfa5f5d5ca4d949221e0228ccc290bacc14e with pinned musl 1.2.6.
Correcting or updating those dependencies would be a declared new configuration,
not an EvoCC compiler patch or an alteration to the locked acceptance result.

